* After defeating the boss in the last mission, you can now continue Rhapsodies of Vanadiel Mission 2-24 {M:The Cursed Temple|The Cursed Temple|The Cursed Temple}.

=2 Walkthrough
* Due to the long nature of this mission, it is recommended that you take precautions to ensure that you have received the {p:key items|Key Item}. This mission can take a while, as it requires travel to a lot of different places, some in the far corners of large and dangerous zones. Always ensure that when checking a headstone you receive the message that you obtained the {p:key item|Key Item}.
* **If you are too far away the game can give you the message, "You need to move closer to {p:key item|Key Item}" and at a quick glance this can appear the same as you acquiring it.** Be sure to double check.
* There are two types of headstones, one type only gives the {p:key item|Key Item}, others spawn {p:NMs|NM} that you must defeat before you may receive the {p:key item|Key Item}.
* Several headstones are close to Cloister home points, it's recommended to grab those on the way if you haven't unlocked them yet.

=3 Non-fights
----
>**Dark Fragment:**
* Obtained upon completion of {M:The Temple of Uggalepih|Zilart Mission 4|The Temple of Uggalepih} from Grav'iton.

----
>**{c=#C68000:Earth Fragment:}**
!Western Altepa Desert.jpg||Western Altepa
!Quicksand Caves-map3.jpg||Quicksand Map 3
* Proceed to (J-9) in {z:Western Altepa Desert}, and enter the {z:Quicksand Caves} (Map 3).
* Head to (K-6) and fall down the sandpit.
* Follow the pathway until you exit back out to {z:Western Altepa Desert}.
** {p:Unity Warp|Unity Concord} 125 {z:Western Altepa Desert} will land you within this area cutting out the need to go through {z:Quicksand Caves}.
** __From the Unity Warp__:
*** Turn around and walk into the crevasse (this cannot be accessed from the outside but the Unity Warp puts you on top of the stone that you cannot normally walk onto.)
*** Follow the path, turning right at the fork until you come to a plunger-looking statue (Ruby Column). Press it down if it is up to continue.
*** Go through the open door near the end of this path and follow it until you exit out at the square shaped crevasse.
*** Turn left and enter the first open door. When you exit again the headstone is located in this section.
* Move in a southwesterly direction towards (H-8)/(H-9) to locate the {p:Cermet Headstone}. Examine it to receive the {@k}{k:Earth fragment}.

----
>**{c=#4996EC:Water Fragment:}**
!La Theine Plateau.jpg||La Theine Plateau
!Ordelle's Caves-map2.jpg||Ordelle's Map 2
!Ordelle's Caves-map1.jpg||Ordelle's Map 1
!Ordelle's Caves-map3.jpg||Ordelle's Map 3
:* __Note: the {p:Geomagnetic Fount} for {z:La Theine Plateau} will let out in the same chasm as the {p:Cermet Headstone}.__

* Proceed to {z:La Theine Plateau} and enter {z:Ordelle's Caves} around (F-7), alternatively you can use Survival Guide to get here. This places you on Map 2.
** Follow the path east to (I-6)(exit B) and you'll switch to Map 1. (East according to map, so left from where you enter.)
** Continue down the tunnel to (G-8).
** From there, go east and enter the south tunnel (exit D) around (H-9).
** Head up the stairs and south until you reach the hole that is at the southside of (H-11), at the transition between (H-11) and (H-12), and go down it. It will be the second hole you come across, not the first.
** Go east to another tunnel (E, Map 3), taking special care not to fall off the cliffs, and head up.
** Once you get to about (I-6), go south.
** Continue on until (H-9) and you'll see a tunnel going west, the zone is not far ahead, bringing you back out to {z:La Theine Plateau}.
*** If you don't have the Geomagnetic-Fount, it will be on the right on a ledge after zoning to the Plateau. Get close to it and interact with it from below to register it.
** The {p:Cermet Headstone} is at the end of the valley at G-11. Examine it to receive the {@k}{k:Water fragment}.

----
>**{c=#00CAF0:Ice Fragment:}**
!Fei'Yin-map1.jpg||Fei'Yin Map 1
!Fei'Yin-map2.jpg||Fei'Yin Map 2
* Make your way to the {z:Cloister of Frost} in the basement of {z:Fei'Yin}. The {p:Cermet Headstone} is in the back of the room. Examine it to receive the {@k}{k:Ice fragment}.
** Fei'Yin Homepoint #2 is right outside the Cloister, if you already have it.
** A level 20+ Summoner can start {q:Trial-Size Trial by Ice|Trial-Size Trial by Ice|Trial-Size Trial by Ice} to be teleported to the Cloister. Don't forget to step outside and grab Fei'Yin Homepoint #2 for later use, especially if you are completing the Trial-Sized quest.

=3 Fights
----
* **{c=red:Fire Fragment:}**

!Yhoator Jungle-map.jpg||Yhoator Jungle
!Headstone Pilgrimage 8bit.png||Cauldron Path
!Yuhtunga Jungle-map.jpg||Yuhtunga Jungle
* **Note**: The one way drops make starting from the {z:Cloister of Flames} or the {z:Ifrit's Cauldron} {p:Homepoint} (i.e. via {i:Mini Fork of Fire|Mini Fork of Fire|1544}) a longer trip that ends up passing the entrance from {z:Yhoator Jungle} / {p:Survival Guide} on Map 4 anyway.
** All three travel options ({s:Teleport-Yhoat}, the {z:Yhoator Jungle} Survival Guide, or the Level 122 Unity Warp) place you around the same area and will allow you to enter {z:Ifrit's Cauldron} as instructed below.
*** Bring a total of 3 {@i:Ice Cluster|4105} {i:Ice Clusters|Ice Cluster|4105} to speed up the flame spouts along the way, if you don't, you'll have to wait up to 3 game hours (around 7 Earth minutes) for them to disappear. Ice Clusters are a common drop from {m:Ice Elementals|Ice Elemental}, which are plentiful in cold zones such as {z:Xarcabard}.
**** Bring {@i:Silent Oil|4165} Silent Oils and {@i:Prism Powder|4164} Prism Powders as bombs will aggro spell casting after removing invisible to trade a cluster.
* Consider taking a {@i:Garnet|790} {i:Garnet|Garnet|790} with you on this leg of the mission, as you can trade it to the headstone to receive the {@i:Opo-opo Necklace|13143} {i:Opo-opo Necklace|Opo-opo Necklace|13143}.
** You need to take the Fire Fragment before doing this.

----
* Enter {z:Ifrit's Cauldron} from (G-6) in {z:Yhoator Jungle}.
** Alternatively take the {p:Survival Guide} warp if you've unlocked it to get to this entrance.
** When you enter, you'll be on Map 4. Head for (H-8) and through the middle exit, and you'll end up on Map 7.
** From Map 7, hug the left wall and head out the exit at (D-12) to continue to Map 5.
** On Map 5, head for (J-8), the only other exit, to get to Map 2. There is a __{c=red:Flame Spout}__ around (H-6)/(H-7). Either wait it out, or trade an {i:Ice Cluster|Ice Cluster|4105}. Waiting it out is safer, but can take extra time.
** On Map 2, run to (E-7) while hugging the left wall, and you'll be back on Map 7. Do not accidentally take the drop that is to the north of the tunnel at (G-8).
** On Map 7, hug the left wall on your way to (G-7) to enter Map 8. Do not accidentally take the drop slightly to the right.
** On Map 8, follow the tunnel to (C-7). This is the exit to {z:Yuhtunga Jungle}. There are two __{c=red:Flame Spouts}__ on the way.
* Near the exit to {z:Yuhtunga Jungle}, you may run across the {m:Ash Dragon}. Your party is likely not able to take it if you are level 75, so be careful.
** During daytime hours (06:00 to 18:00), it's only aggressive to sound. During night time, however, it is True Sound.
*** Take care when passing it, as it will mostly likely spell a wipe for your party.
* Once outside, gather everyone up and head for the tunnel under the waterfall at (K-7). The headstone is located around (L-6)/(L-7). Check the {p:Cermet Headstone} to spawn two {p:Opo-opo|Category:Opo-opo} {p:NMs|NM}, {m:Carthi} and {m:Tipha}.
** They will both aggro through sneak and cannot be {s:slept|Sleep}, but are susceptible to gravity and bind.
** Defeat both Opos and check the {p:Cermet Headstone} again to receive the {@k}{k:Fire fragment}.
*** If you get a message saying "Don't you have something better to do right now?", keep checking the headstone until you get the KI.

----
>**{c=#BC4EC8:Lightning Fragment:}**
!Behemoth's Dominion-map.jpg||Behemoth's Dominion
* Travel to {z:Behemoth's Dominion} (G-9).
** Unity Warp Level 135 will be the fastest way to get here.
* Clear the area of mobs and check the headstone to spawn two {p:Weapon|Category:Evil Weapon} NMs: {m:Legendary Weapon} (BLM/RDM) and {m:Ancient Weapon} (WAR).
** Defeat them both and check the {p:Cermet Headstone} again to receive the {@k}{k:Lightning fragment}.
* It is possible to fight only one of the {p:NMs|NM}, by using the {s:Sneak}-pull method. {s:Sneak} one member, pull one of the {p:NMs|NM} and wait for the other to de-pop. Defeat the original and proceed.
** Both are susceptible to {s:Bind} and {s:Gravity}, but not sleep or silence.
** Both will use their 1-hour abilities around 50%.
*** Legendary Weapon will use Manafont and begin casting back-to-back.
**** Casts Diaga 2, Paralyze, Silence, Slow, Gravity, Cure IV, Protect/Shell, etc.
*** Either can be defeated solo at level 75 with DoT and occasional nukes while kiting it around the {m:King Behemoth} spawn area.
**** {m:Ancient Weapon} is not {p:aspirable|Aspir}, but the {m:Legendary Weapon} is.

----
>**{c=#00C900:Wind Fragment:}**
!Cape Teriggan - Map.jpg||Cape Teriggan
* Consider taking a {@i:Rain Lily|949} {i:Rain Lily|Rain Lily|949} with you on this part of the mission. Trading it to the headstone will earn you a {@i:Flagellant's Rope|13248} {i:Flagellant's Rope|Flagellant's Rope|13248}.
** You need to take the Wind Fragment before doing this.
* Start off for {z:Cape Teriggan}, both the {p:Home Point} and Unity Warp 128 let out close to the {p:Cermet Headstone}.
* Head for (F-7) and locate the unmarked hidden tunnel (it is in the same general area as the tunnel to get to the {z:Cloister of Gales}).
** Go north until you come out into another open area, taking another hidden tunnel at (G-5).
*** Follow it until (H-5), where the headstone is located.
* Check the headstone to pop a {p:Shadow|Category:Fomor} {p:NM} named {m:Axesarion the Wanderer}.
** Defeat it and check the {p:Cermet Headstone} again to receive the {@k}{k:Wind fragment}.

----
>**{c=gray:Light Fragment:}**
!The Sanctuary of Zi'Tah-map.jpg||The Sanctuary of Zi'Tah
* Proceed to {z:The Sanctuary of Zi'Tah}. Your goal is to get to (J-9) first.
** The {p:Survival Guide}/Outpost warp will get you closest to (J-9).
* From (J-9), entrance is at the South Eastern (SE) corner of the box, hug left wall till you're near the North Eastern corner of (I-7).
** This is the same area where {m:Keeper of Halidom} can spawn.
* Check the headstone to spawn a {p:Doomed|Category:Doomed} {p:NM} named {m:Doomed Pilgrims}.
** This {p:NM} hits fairly fast and hard, but should pose little trouble to a well balanced party of 65+.
* Defeat the {p:NM} and check the {p:Cermet Headstone} again to receive the {@k}{k:Light fragment}.
* **Note**: Come back to this headstone after completing {M:ZM7: The Chamber of Oracles|Zilart Mission 7|The Chamber of Oracles} to receive a {@i:Bat Earring|13416} {i:Bat Earring|Bat Earring|13416}.

----
* Upon obtaining the final fragment, you will receive the message, "You now have all 8 fragments of light!" and the mission will be complete.

